ST-Map packages the runtime dependency closure of ST-CogNav at commit
5ac93986c2db14d9f25143d86ed0b55ad7f8735c
("ST-CogNav memory: archive removed objects and extract prompt subgraph").

UPSTREAM.json records SHA-256 hashes of the original selected source blobs.
Files have integration changes: local imports are namespaced, configuration and
resources are relocatable, credentials are removed, lifecycle is adapted, and
runtime edge cases are repaired. Temporal-memory and voxel-coordinate methods
have been moved into st_map.memory and st_map.geometry.

Original copyright and attribution notices are retained in vendored files,
including notices for OpenSeeD, Detectron2/Mask2Former, Deformable DETR,
Swin Transformer, and TensorFlow-derived depth utilities. External dependencies
and separately downloaded model weights retain their respective licenses.
The parent checkout does not provide a separate upstream LICENSE file; this
notice does not relicense third-party code or model weights.

Code that never runs in UniNavBench was removed after packaging: unused modules (alternative OpenSeeD
backbones and decoders, drawing and visualization helpers), functions and imports that no executed
or referenced code reaches, and commented-out code. Comments were translated to English.
The OpenSeeD detection vocabulary (configs/panoptic_categories_nomerge.txt) is extended with the ProcTHOR
object types of the benchmark that it lacked (e.g. tv stand, credit card, salt shaker).
